"""Present the analytical spin-three bound and its sharp N18 consequence."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(tex,display=True):
 tag='div'if display else'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(tex,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(url,quote=True)}">{label} ↗</a>'for url,label in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 upper=json.loads((HERE/'upper-verification.json').read_text());ind=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());lower=json.loads((HERE/'witness-verification.json').read_text());assert upper['passed']and ind['passed']and lower['passed']
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)+'\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent subspaces · Analytical optimality proof</p><a href="../../index.html#n=18&t=4">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Eighteen qubits: fourth-order AC subspaces have dimension at most one</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex subspaces</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(18,4)=1.}')+'<p>A spin-three auxiliary system gives a short exclusion of every AC4 plane. The existing exact fifth-order state supplies an attaining fourth-order line.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>A quartic with thirteen positive eigenvalues</h2><p>Let '+m(r'\mathcal C\subset V_9',False)+' be a fourth-order AC subspace of dimension '+m(r'k',False)+', with projector '+m(r'P',False)+'. Couple the physical spin nine to auxiliary spin three:</p>'+m(r'X=\mathbf J\cdot\mathbf S=\sum_{a=x,y,z}J_a\otimes S_a.')+'<p>Use the centered quartic</p>'+m(r'\begin{aligned}W&=(X+23)(X+6)(X-4)(X-27)-6264I\\&=X^4-2X^3-653X^2-1146X+8640I.\end{aligned}')
 b+='<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Total spin '+m(r'L',False)+'</th><th>Multiplicity</th><th>Eigenvalue of '+m(r'W',False)+'</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
 for L,v in zip(range(6,13),[319320,-6264,-63720,-6264,-6264,-111600,-6264]):b+=f'<tr><td>{L}</td><td>{2*L+1}</td><td>{v}</td></tr>'
 b+='</tbody></table></div><p>The physical partial trace vanishes exactly:</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_{V_9}W=0.')+'<p>The only positive sector has total spin six and dimension thirteen; all remaining 120 eigenvalues are strictly negative.</p></section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Why an AC4 plane is impossible</h2><p>Fourth-order anticoherence of the whole subspace, including cross terms, gives</p>'+m(r'PAP=\frac{\operatorname{Tr}A}{19}P')+'<p>for every physical-spin polynomial '+m(r'A',False)+' of degree at most four. Applying this to each physical coefficient of '+m(r'W',False)+' yields</p>'+m(r'(P\otimes I_7)W(P\otimes I_7)=\frac{P}{19}\otimes\operatorname{Tr}_{V_9}W=0.')+'<p>Thus '+m(r'\mathcal C\otimes V_3',False)+' is a totally isotropic subspace of dimension '+m(r'7k',False)+'. Its projection into the positive spectral subspace must be injective: a nonzero vector with no positive component would have strictly negative quadratic form. Therefore</p>'+m(r'\boxed{7k\le13\quad\Longrightarrow\quad k\le1.}')+'<p>This argument uses every complex subspace and imposes no symmetry or Dicke-support restriction.</p></section>'
 b+='<section><h2>An exact state attains dimension one</h2>'+m(r'\begin{aligned}\sqrt{130}|\psi\rangle={}&\sqrt{14}(|D_{18}^{(0)}\rangle+|D_{18}^{(18)}\rangle)\\&+i\sqrt{51}(|D_{18}^{(5)}\rangle+|D_{18}^{(13)}\rangle).\end{aligned}')+'<p>The normalized Dicke coefficients are already present in the supplied Julia source and pure AC-state catalogue. Its fourth reduced state is '+m(r'I_5/5',False)+'. It also has fifth-order anticoherence, so its line attains the optimal dimension at both orders.</p>'+links([('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=18&t=4&state=acliege-n18-t5','Matching pure-state witness'),('../n18-t5/index.html','Fifth-order state and dimension proof'),('witness-verification.json','Exact lower-bound verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>A general fourth-order upper bound</h2>'+m(r'\boxed{7K(N,t)\le N-5\qquad(N\ge16,\ t\ge4).}')+'<p>For '+m(r'j=N/2',False)+' and the same spin-three auxiliary system, take</p>'+m(r'F_j(X)=(X+2j+5)(X+6)(X-j+5)(X-3j),')+m(r'c_j=2j(4j^3-36j^2+47j-75),\qquad W=F_j(X)-c_jI.')+'<p>Its physical partial trace is zero. For '+m(r'h=j-8\ge0',False)+',</p>'+m(r'c_j=2j(4h^3+60h^2+239h+45)>0.')+'<p>The quartic is nonpositive at every coupling eigenvalue except the lowest. After centering, the only positive sector is '+m(r'L=j-3',False)+', of dimension '+m(r'N-5',False)+'. The same injective-projection argument proves the bound. The catalogue applies it to every displayed cell in its domain. At nineteen qubits it gives '+m(r'7k\le14',False)+'. A separate <a href="../n19-t4/exclusion/index.html">exact four-copy certificate</a> now proves '+m(r'K(19,4)=1',False)+'.</p></section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Reproducible exact checks</h2><p>Two independent physical-matrix calculations verify the spectrum and zero partial trace. The attaining state is checked with exact normalized-Dicke reductions. No numerical eigenvalue or failed optimization is used in the proof.</p>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact polynomial and spectrum'),('verify_upper.py','Exact upper-bound verifier'),('upper-verification.json','Upper verification'),('verify_independently.py','Independent normalized-spin audit'),('independent-verification.json','Independent report'),('verify_witness.py','Exact witness verifier'),('positive-control.json','Numerical diagnostic controls')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=18: maximum fourth-order AC dimension is one</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
